            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for to get wet, then the Urdu for to travel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: گولی",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گولی — golī — \"a pill; a bullet\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گولی (golī) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from golikā, \"little ball\" (CDIAL 4321). It is built on gola, \"ball\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
